nding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though the docstring said otherwise.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. With this fix, `2.665` now rounds to `2.66`, as the test expects.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR opened, but its reviewer list came back empty, so I'll request alex directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EjQ7db89dAqrAnj1J7Zq14", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex as the reviewer. CI passed on the fix.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says FIN-212 requires `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (banker's rounding). So `2.665` rounded to `2.67`, but the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`). Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. Opening the PR didn't add alex as a reviewer, so I requested his review separately, and he's now on it.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}